!: 2003 nuclear masses: 
!: Q-value= 0.763 803 MeV
!: Ethr   = 1.019 044
!: Edbl   = 1.147 327
!: Ethrd-d= 5.382 605
!: Ethrdbu= 8.354 324 
!: Ethrbu =11.327 803
!:
!: 20110228: between 1.20 MeV and 6.50 MeV 3He(n,p)-data from ENDF/B-VII.0
!: 20000126: below 1.02 MeV shape from 3He(n,p) ENDF/B-6
!: 1999-06-06: below 1.8 MeV integrated values taken from HALE99; this is 
!: indicated by two leading zeros at the energies! If energies are given
!: by seven digits, data are straight from HALE99.
!: from 2.0 to 3.2 MeV adjustment to SHAPE of integrated data of BRUNE.
!: This is indicated by one leading zero.
!!: There is a step in the excitation function below 2 MeV of -1.08%. 
!: The higher energy data are already low with regard to the accurate data 
!: of Jarmie (1.11%), so that lowering those is not justified at this point.
!: (see also 1991-09-xx)
!: 1999-05-15: 13.6 MeV added (by interpolation)
!: 1994-05-03: at 2.2, 2.6 & 6.5 MeV sum of coeff. changed by 0.0002 - added
!:             11.5 to avoid sum of coefficients .ne. 1.
!: 1993: there is an indication from t-H2O data that between 6.0126 and 6.6807 
!  MeV the evaluated cross sections should be raised at 
!: 180 and 148.4 - 148.55 deg by as much as 3 %.
!: 1991-09-xx: p-T and d-D appear to be low by (1.51 +- 0.35%) at 13.6 and 
!: 12.305 MeV, resp., when compared with the reference data of Jarmie, whereas 
!: d-T between 10 to 14 MeV appears to be high by (1.49 +- 0.46)% 
!: when compared with the scales of Jarmie, Ivanovich and Stewart.
!: 1990-06-04: Data below 1.3 MeV modified using G. Hale's R-Matrix predictions 
!: 1985: evaluation from 1.2 (1.4) to 16.0 MeV from LA-10444/ IAEA Handbook
!: NOTE: 0 degree excitation function above 40 MeV does NOT match data below
!: 33 MeV

!: ATTENTION: the code assumes that a given coefficient is zero if at any 
!: higher energy there are no nonzero coefficients of the same or a higher 
!: order!!!
!: If single angle data (e.g. 0 deg, 180 deg) are added to Legendre tables the
!: following steps must be taken:
C1: Add min. energy(EMINL) and maximum energy(EMAXL) of Legendre values in 
!: 1st line
C2: make first added energy value EMAXL+0.1 keV
C3: give AT LEAST 5 additional energy values
